### What is the problem?

Palindrome Partitioning — backtrack with palindrome check at each cut. Given a string, partition it so that every substring of the partition is a palindrome, and return all possible palindrome partitionings.

### How does the approach work?

Carry a start index and a path of substrings. When start equals the length, record a copy of the path. Otherwise loop end from start to the end; if substring start..end is a palindrome, add it, recurse from end+1, and remove it. For example: `if (isPalindrome(s,start,end)) { path.add(s.substring(start,end+1)); backtrack(end+1); path.remove(last); }`.

The palindrome check uses two pointers moving inward. For better performance you can precompute a boolean DP table isPal[i][j] so each check is O(1), making the overall cost dominated by the number of partitions.

The worst-case time is O(n · 2^n) because a string of all identical characters has 2^(n-1) partitions, each of length up to n. A senior nuance is that the DP precomputation turns repeated palindrome checks from O(n) each into O(1), which matters on adversarial inputs.

### What is the banking use case?

Problem 1 — At National Bank of India, a legacy reference code must be split into symmetric segments for a validation scheme, and the tool needs every valid segmentation. This is exactly how palindrome partitioning works.

Problem 2 — A segment is only acceptable if it is a palindrome, and the segments together must cover the whole code. This is exactly why each prefix is palindrome-checked before recursing on the remainder.

The mini-project builds a `ReferenceSegmenter`, a `BankLogFormatter`, and a runnable demo.

### How do you implement this in Java?

```java
// ─── File: src/main/java/com/bank/refval/ReferenceSegmenter.java ───
package com.bank.refval;

import java.util.ArrayList;
import java.util.List;
import java.util.logging.Logger;

public class ReferenceSegmenter {

    private static final Logger log = Logger.getLogger(ReferenceSegmenter.class.getName());

    public List<List<String>> partition(String s) {
        List<List<String>> result = new ArrayList<>();
        backtrack(s, 0, new ArrayList<>(), result);
        log.info(() -> "Found " + result.size() + " palindrome segmentations of '" + s + "'");
        return result;
    }

    private void backtrack(String s, int start, List<String> path, List<List<String>> result) {
        if (start == s.length()) { result.add(new ArrayList<>(path)); return; }
        for (int end = start; end < s.length(); end++) {
            if (isPalindrome(s, start, end)) {         // keep only palindromic prefix
                path.add(s.substring(start, end + 1));
                backtrack(s, end + 1, path, result);
                path.remove(path.size() - 1);
            }
        }
    }

    private boolean isPalindrome(String s, int lo, int hi) {
        while (lo < hi) {
            if (s.charAt(lo++) != s.charAt(hi--)) return false;
        }
        return true;
    }
}
```

